mod:addr_via_pointer_deep_faces_3;
// 2026-11-18 (landing 177d2c, row 1: DEF-644 root B at every depth). An address taken through a pointer names storage that pointer points at, and
// 177d2b9's row 3 rerooted it ONE level. Where a target is itself a place through a pointer (`r3 = @(<-r)` over `r = @((<-q0).inner)`; `sp =
// @(<-sp1)` over `sp1 = @(<-sp2)`), its root's chain is still a pointer's own, so a store landing two or more levels down went unrecorded: by the
// record, by the store's descents, on the two rootless roads, or through V's held arms at the last hop. A growth of what was stored then freed
// what the place read. The escape analysis now walks every place such an address reaches (`reroot_closure`: a worklist with a memo, a fold by
// full ref, a per-call stamp, bounded by the tree with a guard that fails closed), and the record, `rrti_path`'s and `rrti_chain`'s descents, the
// rootless destination, a storing callee's rootless pointer argument and V's last-hop arms all read it. A fix only adds records beside main's.
// THE FACES (169), each a fault on R3F (524cf77), refused here, each once by text. C1Fb's (145's and 146's): `r26_2lv`, `r26_3lv`, `r26_3lv_n`,
// `r26_dd`, `r26_fld`, `r26_pp`, `r26_sbf`, `cal_st3`, `cal_stq2`, `cst_in`, `cyc_loop`, `cyc_rr`, `cyc_self`, `cyc_two`, `dd3`, `dd4`, `dd5`,
// `dd6`, `dd7`, `mix5`, `nul_bang`, `nul_dflt`, `nul_mid`, `perf_cyc`, `perf_wide`, `qq3`, `qq4`, `qq5`, `qq6`, `tp_br`, `tp_br_y`, `tp_diam`,
// `tp_join`, `tp_two`, `dd10`, `dd11`, `dd12`, `dd13`, `dd14`, `dd15`, `dd8`, `dd9`, `a5_hpc`, `a5_if`, `a5_loop`, `a5_rsg`, `a5_view`,
// `fu_alt130`, `fu_alt40`, `fu_alt62`, `fu_alt63`, `fu_alt64`, `fu_alt65`, `fu_alt70`, `fu_alt8`, `fu_self130`, `fu_self40`, `fu_self62`,
// `fu_self63`, `fu_self64`, `fu_self65`, `fu_self70`, `fu_self8`, `mt_un1`, `mt_un2`, `mt_un3`, `mt_cp1`, `mt_cp2`, `mt_cp3`, `mt_cu1`, `mt_cu2`,
// `mt_cu3`, `d_res2`, `d_res3`, `d_tern2`. C1Fc's, by piece: (a) the descents, `t_pb2`, `t_pb3`, `v_2h2`, `w_2h2`, `w_2h2a`, `w_2h3`, `w_3h2`,
// `w_c2pp`, `w_pp2`, `w_pp3`, `g_cy3`, `g_dup`; (b) the rootless roads, `rc_c1`, `rc_c2`, `rc_t1`, `rc_t2`, `rl_2h1`, `rl_2h2`, `rl_pp1`,
// `rl_pp2`, `t_rlp2`, `t_rlp3`, `g_rlcy2`; (c) V at the last hop, `t_v1h1`, `t_v1h1a`, `t_v1h2`, `t_vm1`, `t_vm2`, `t_vme1`, `t_vpp1`, `t_vpp2`,
// `g_vcy2`, `g_vmcy`. Piece (c)'s from 148's attack: `kp_V`, `kp_M`, `s_ks_V`, `s_ks_M`, `s_s_V`, `s_s_M`. `fz3_429`, which pins the memo's drops
// together: with no drop it is accepted. Piece (c)'s price shape read on a fresh local after the store, so the price's hold is gone and the
// growth is refused: `kp_Vd`, `kp_Md`, `s_ks_Vd`, `s_ks_Md`. 148's verdict sweeps by class, one per set and road (22 here, of the 2,307 cells of
// its sets s1, s2, s3 and sx that move from accepted on R3F to refused here; the rest are named by count in the record): `s1_s_Y_A`, `s1_s_Y_B`,
// `s1_s_Y_C`, `s1_s_Y_D`, `s1_s_Y_E`, `s1_s_F_L`, `s1_s_Y_R`, `s1_s_F_T`, `s1_s_Y_W`, `s2_s_FF_A`, `s2_s_FF_B`, `s2_s_FF_C`, `s2_s_FF_D`,
// `s2_s_FF_E`, `s2_s_FF_L`, `s2_s_FF_R`, `s2_s_FF_T`, `s2_s_FF_W`, `s3_s_FFF_C`, `s3_s_FFF_L`, `s3_s_FFF_V`, `s3_s_FFF_W`. 146's cells that row
// 1's census found closed, from its sections 1 and 5 and its fuzz: `d_cal2`, `d_fld2`, `fz1_1`, `fz3_47`, `fz3_77`, `fz4_102`, `fz4_271`,
// `fz4_313`, `fz5_183`, `fz5_230`, `fz6_467`, `pd2_o`, `pd3x_o`, `rc_n2`, `rs_2d`, `um_c3`, `um_l3b`, `um_p2`, `um_p3`, `um_s3b`, `um_s4`,
// `ur_b2`, `w_b1`, `w_b2`, `w_mem2`, `w_mem3`, `w_mid2`. And `pdc_o`, a fault on R3F only from 5 arguments on (its callee re-aims the pointer
// when n > 5), so its runs take 0 to 8 arguments.
// 2026-11-19 (landing 177d2d, row 2: row 1 of 177d2c held out, now rebased onto aefae6e as R1-4 with the cost fix, its price DEF-694; rulings l.19112 and l.19370):
